# After-Sales Repair Order

## Navigation

- **After-Sales** is a **top-level sidebar module** (`after_sales` in [`modules.ts`](web/src/shell/modules.ts)), sibling to Inventory — not an Inventory sub-branch.
- Feature tabs (Repair Order List, New Repair Order, Register Repair, etc.) render in the **sticky header** via the standard module feature nav in [`AppShell.tsx`](web/src/shell/AppShell.tsx).
- Base path: `/app/after-sales`. Legacy `/app/inventory/after-sales/*` URLs redirect to the new paths.

## Numbering (per tenant, per calendar day)

- **Date-no display:** `MM/DD/YYYY-#` from `order_date` + `date_seq`.
- **Repair Order No.:** `YYMMDD` + 9-digit zero-padded daily counter (e.g. `260616000000001`).
- Allocated atomically via `allocate_repair_order_sequences()` in migration `007_repair_orders.sql`.

## Grid golden rules

- **+ New row** opens [`RepairOrderModal`](web/src/modules/inventory/after-sales/RepairOrderModal.tsx).
- **Cog icon** → `/app/after-sales/repair-orders/settings` (`EntityFormSettingsPage`).
- **Print** (Receipt) and **Warranty** (Details) open print views in a new tab; data from `GET /api/v1/inventory/repair-orders/{id}/print?doc=receipt|warranty`.

## Repair Order Status report

- Route: `/app/after-sales/repair-orders/status` — filter first (F8), then line-level grid.
- **Date-No** click → `RepairOrderModal`. **Progress** inline → `PATCH .../progress-status`.
- Line **remark** column: migration `008_repair_order_status.sql`; editable in `EditableLineGrid`.
- Print: `/repair-orders/status/print?...` (browser print). Excel: `GET .../status-report/export`.

## Item picker

- Double-click **Item Code** in [`EditableLineGrid`](web/src/shared/EditableLineGrid.tsx) → [`ItemSearchModal`](web/src/shared/ItemSearchModal.tsx).
- **Submit-to-search only** — `POST /api/v1/inventory/items/search`; no live filter-as-you-type.
- Extended item columns live in migration `006_item_master_extended.sql`.

## API

- `GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE /api/v1/inventory/repair-orders`
- `GET /api/v1/inventory/repair-orders/preview-sequences?order_date=YYYY-MM-DD`
- `GET /api/v1/inventory/repair-orders/status-report` (line-level, filtered)
- `GET /api/v1/inventory/repair-orders/status-report/export` (CSV)
- `PATCH /api/v1/inventory/repair-orders/{id}/progress-status`
- `GET /api/v1/inventory/after-sales/users?q=` (PIC lookup)

## Permissions

- Module code: `after_sales` (migration `025_after_sales_module.sql`).
- Feature permission codes: `after_sales.repair_orders`, `after_sales.register_repair`, etc.
